{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel>\n    <data id=\"seen\" expr=\"[]\"/>\n  </datamodel>\n  <script src=\"scripts/side-effects.js\"/>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <onentry>\n      <log label=\"seen\" expr=\"remember('entry')\"/>\n    </onentry>\n    <transition event=\"go\" target=\"f\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"f\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml074-script-src-side-effect.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":1,"notes":0,"total":1,"warnings":0},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"error","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml074-script-src-side-effect.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":48,"endLine":8,"startColumn":31,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`expr` on `<log>` has a side effect\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §4.7.3: \"The SCXML processor MUST ensure that <log> has no side-effects on document interpretation.\"\n\n**Help:** log a value without changing anything; move the change into `<assign>` or `<script>`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 Appendix B Data Models\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §4.7.3 <log>\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`expr` on `<log>` has a side effect"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":278,"start":261},"category":"semantic"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"`remember` calls the mutating `push` here (in `scripts/side-effects.js`)"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml074-script-src-side-effect.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":5,"startColumn":16,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML074"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"error"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §4.7.3: \"The SCXML processor MUST ensure that <log> has no side-effects on document interpretation.\" An ECMAScript `<log>` value is an ECMAScript expression (B.2), which can assign, so the validator rejects one that certainly changes state outside itself when it runs: an assignment, update, or `delete` of a variable or property outside the expression, a built-in method that changes its receiver or argument (`push`, `sort`, `Object.assign`, ...), `Math.random` (the session's random sequence advances), or a call of a document function whose body does one of those"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: log a value without changing anything, and move the change into executable content (`<assign>` or `<script>`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §4.7.3 <log>\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML074` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#log","id":"SCXML074","name":"SCXML074","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a `<log expr>` has a side effect"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}